     "do": [
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "stages"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Why execute out of order, the scoreboard's four steps, and its units and tables."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "stages[0..=2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Then the textbook example cycle by cycle, a snapshot of the tables, the WAR stall, the limits, and an exam question."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "stages[3..=7]"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "why",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 1: a divide takes 40 cycles. The add needs its result, so the add must wait."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 1 of 8: why out of order"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "stages"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "why"
      },
      {
       "action": "goto_line",
       "target": "why",
       "line": 2
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "But the subtract needs nothing from either. In an in-order pipeline it is stuck behind the add anyway, for 40 cycles."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "goto_line",
       "target": "why",
       "line": 3
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Compare the two ways of running it."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "why"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "whyx"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "whyx[0][1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Dynamic scheduling lets the subtract go ahead. Instructions issue in order, but execute as soon as their operands are ready."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "whyx[0][2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The price: once instructions finish out of order, WAR and WAW hazards become real. If the subtract wrote F8 before the add had read it, the add would get the wrong value."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "whyx[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "So the hardware must track every instruction in flight. That bookkeeping is the scoreboard."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "issue in order · execute out of order · watch for RAW, WAR and WAW"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "steps",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 2: the scoreboard splits the decode stage in two, and every instruction passes through four steps."
